  "pages": [
    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:reality_compiler",
      "title": "Reality Compiler",
      "text": "Bostrom asked whether we live in a simulation. The $(item)Reality Compiler$() takes it literally: if the universe is a simulation, this decompiles it.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 6$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "This controller is too complex for a crafting grid. Build it on the $(item)Femtoscale Assembly Line$() - check JEI for the exact parts."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "The final machine. Decompile reality into $(item)Source Code Fragments$(), forge $(item)Reality Anchors$(), and finally compile the $(item)Omega Point$() - which a Zero-Point Extractor can burn for 10 hours.$(br2)If I am wrong about the simulation, the error messages will be very interesting."
    },
